Scope the repair pass to one backend, and stop counting 404s as errors

Caught by running the sweep and reading its report instead of the headline: it
said "repaired 2" and also "errors 6", and the six were not noise.

Of seven candidates, six were the OLD backend's rows (runs 2091-2097). This pass
repairs a row from whatever run comes back for its id - and a run id identifies
a call only within one backend. Today those ids merely 404 on Vaani, because
Vaani is at ~800. That is a clock, not a fix: when Vaani reaches 2091 they stop
404-ing and start returning a DIFFERENT customer's call, which this pass would
then merge into an August row.

Exactly the collision scripts/009 exists for, reintroduced in the repair path I
had just written. It has to be handled everywhere a run id is treated as an
identity, not only at insert. The candidate query is now scoped by provider, so
the wrong-backend question is never asked.

A 404 is also reclassified as skipped rather than error: it means "no such run
on this backend", a normal outcome. Left as an error it reported six permanent
failures every tick and would have hidden a real one.

